{"kind":"promise","text":"I will state the job gitseq does, add the solo-adoption route, and quote the standing prompt verbatim, on branch request/state-the-job.\n\nMeasured against what main carries now, part of this request is already satisfied and I am not going to re-do it or claim credit for it. README.md was last edited at 7d97348d on 2026-08-10 12:15, an hour after this request was filed at 11:04, and that edit moved the job statement to the top: the README now opens on a multi-agent workspace and the document-currency argument follows it under \"Why\", which is the ordering this request asked for. What the opening does not yet carry is hugh's specific framing — your own local agents, each with its own skills, coordinating around one development project, and gitseq as the do-it-yourself way to get there. I will sharpen that, not rewrite it.\n\nThe prompt is present but paraphrased. Line 26 reads \"Using the gitseq MCP, check for work items and prioritize appropriately to keep progressing.\" Hugh's words are \"Using the gitseq mcp server, check for work items and prioritize appropriately to keep work progressing.\" The request says verbatim, and a standing instruction that agents are meant to copy is exactly the wrong place to improve someone's wording, so I will restore it exactly.\n\nThe solo-adoption route is genuinely missing and is the substance of this work. Every entry path starts from an empty directory: docs/getting-started.md line 41, docs/how-to/end-to-end.md line 37, and four other how-to pages all open with mktemp -d. Nothing covers running gs init inside a repository you already work in, which leaves the impression that adopting gitseq requires the organization to agree first. I will add that path and link it from the README and getting-started.\n\nConditions I hold myself to: the how-to pages are executed by the gates, so any commands I add must actually run against a repository with existing history rather than a scratch directory; make test, make docs and the docset gate pass; the worktree is clean; and the head is zero commits behind main and merges clean before I ask anyone to review it. I will run the docset gate alone on this machine, because concurrent runs contend on a fixed port."}